# Store text with LF in the repository, and check it out in each platform's own form.
# Without this the tree is authored on Windows with CRLF while CI runs on Linux, and
# every file reads as wholly rewritten in a cross-platform diff. `text=auto` leaves the
# working copy alone on Windows -- it normalises what is committed, not what you edit.
* text=auto

# Amira spatial graphs and lattices, image stacks and surfaces are binary; a newline
# conversion would silently corrupt them.
*.am     binary
*.stl    binary
*.tif    binary
*.tiff   binary
*.npz    binary
*.pkl    binary

# Long-form docs and generated reports do not belong in a language breakdown of the
# repository, and the docs are prose rather than code.
**/docs/**            linguist-documentation
packages/*/PORTING.md linguist-documentation
# One-off diagnostics kept for reproducibility, not shipped code.
packages/coronary_sdf/research_scripts/** linguist-vendored
